    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T15:59:56Z",
    "body": "Readings on main `d1484f02a` (plate 60 x 60 x [0, 10], through hole D20 with 32 chords, EM-0600-4FL D6, stepdown 2.5, stock box 70 x 70 x 11):\n\n- **Depth cause.** `contour_depth::ladder` tests each level against the part material strictly above the plane. At Z 10 (the part top) no material is above, so each ring is legal there. At Z 7.5 the Outside ring (r 12.99, 3 mm into the plate) is in material, and the ladder stops. No vertex plane is between 10 and 7.5. The ring walks only Z 10, with the note \"the part is solid below it; levels below skipped (7.500, 5.000, 2.500, 0.000)\". The ladder is not empty, so the refusal \"every contour ring cuts into the part at its first level\" does not fire. That refusal fires only when the top height is below the part top.\n- **Full depth.** Top of model to Bottom of model 0 gives the same result: one level at Z 10, status Ok, 0 warnings, 0 gouges, posted. A patch pick with selection heights gives the same result.\n- **What the path does.** The tip stays on the top face. The path does not cut into the wall. It is a silent pass in the wrong place, not a 3D gouge. The \"points inside the part\" are the 2D footprint at the top plane.\n- **Verifier.** `verify` (Boundary mode, model = plate facets) on the Outside ring, forced down the full ladder, reports Gouge warnings on each move below Z 10. The verifier finds the real gouge. I filed no verifier issue.\n- **Inside and Auto** on the same hole walk all levels 10, 7.5, 5, 2.5, 0 at r 6.985, clean, posted.\n\nFix: a picked ring (Selection source) that walks no level below the local part top, while the operation levels go below that top, is refused by name at generation. The whole-model source does not change.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
